WEBVTT

00:00.730 --> 00:01.690
- [Instructor] We're told that Marvin

00:01.690 --> 00:04.200
has an inflatable wading
pool in his back yard.

00:04.200 --> 00:06.530
The pool is cylindrical with a base area

00:06.530 --> 00:09.920
of four square meters and
a height of 60 centimeters.

00:09.920 --> 00:13.590
What is the volume of
the pool in cubic meters?

00:13.590 --> 00:16.253
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:17.110 --> 00:18.450
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:18.450 --> 00:20.070
And let's just first visualize

00:20.070 --> 00:23.920
what this cylindrical
wading pool would look like.

00:23.920 --> 00:25.180
It would look something like this.

00:25.180 --> 00:26.710
A wading pool's kind of a small pool

00:26.710 --> 00:28.440
where you can just hang out a bit in it.

00:28.440 --> 00:31.620
You're not necessarily gonna
swim around too much in it.

00:31.620 --> 00:35.020
So it might look something like this.

00:35.020 --> 00:36.360
I know I'm not drawing it perfectly.

00:36.360 --> 00:38.090
It's kind of a hand-drawn situation,

00:38.090 --> 00:42.190
and I'm making it transparent
so that we can see the base.

00:42.190 --> 00:44.320
So the wading pool would
look something like that.

00:44.320 --> 00:48.750
They tell us that we have a
base area of four square meters.

00:48.750 --> 00:53.150
So this area right over
here, that's the base.

00:53.150 --> 00:55.490
That is four square meters.

00:55.490 --> 00:57.920
And it has a height of 60 centimeters,

00:57.920 --> 00:59.420
tell us that right over there.

00:59.420 --> 01:03.190
So this height is 60 centimeters.

01:03.190 --> 01:05.447
So the volume, our
reaction might be to say,

01:05.447 --> 01:08.636
"Okay, the volume of a cylinder
is the area of the base

01:08.636 --> 01:10.470
times the height."

01:10.470 --> 01:12.040
And so in this case,

01:12.040 --> 01:15.963
why wouldn't we just take four times 60,

01:16.840 --> 01:21.790
times 60, and we would
get a volume of 240.

01:21.790 --> 01:23.210
And we want it in cubic meters,

01:23.210 --> 01:25.580
so we just say 240 cubic meters.

01:25.580 --> 01:26.480
Is this true?

01:26.480 --> 01:28.476
Did I just do this correctly?

01:28.476 --> 01:30.850
Well, some of you might have realized

01:30.850 --> 01:31.990
that what I just multiplied,

01:31.990 --> 01:33.800
I didn't multiply four square meters

01:33.800 --> 01:37.450
times 60 meters to get 240 cubic meters.

01:37.450 --> 01:39.710
I just multiplied four square meters

01:39.710 --> 01:43.710
times 60, 60 centimeters.

01:43.710 --> 01:45.450
And if you multiply these two things,

01:45.450 --> 01:47.540
your actual units would
not be cubic meters.

01:47.540 --> 01:50.590
You would end up of units of
meters squared centimeters,

01:50.590 --> 01:51.710
which is not what they want

01:51.710 --> 01:54.320
and that is kind of a
bizarre set of units.

01:54.320 --> 01:56.890
So in order to get the
answer in cubic meters,

01:56.890 --> 02:01.820
we would wanna re-express 60
centimeters in terms of meters.

02:01.820 --> 02:05.450
Well, how many meters is 60 centimeters?

02:05.450 --> 02:08.480
Well, 100 centimeters make a meter.

02:08.480 --> 02:10.090
So I could write it this way.

02:10.090 --> 02:15.090
So 100 centimeters equal one meter.

02:17.280 --> 02:18.850
Or another way you could think about it is

02:18.850 --> 02:23.850
one centimeter is equal
to 1/100 of a meter.

02:25.870 --> 02:29.280
And so 60 centimeters is going to be equal

02:29.280 --> 02:34.210
to 60/100 of a meter.

02:34.210 --> 02:35.580
So now we can apply this,

02:35.580 --> 02:39.100
'cause we're dealing with
meters consistently now.

02:39.100 --> 02:41.530
So we can say, so this is actually wrong.

02:41.530 --> 02:43.350
We could say the volume
is going to be equal

02:43.350 --> 02:45.780
to the base in square meters,

02:45.780 --> 02:46.780
and I'm gonna write the units down

02:46.780 --> 02:48.380
and make sure we're doing the right thing,

02:48.380 --> 02:53.380
times the height, times
60 over 100 meters.

02:55.460 --> 02:57.570
And now everything works out.

02:57.570 --> 03:02.570
Four times 60 over 100 is
going to be 240 over 100.

03:04.260 --> 03:06.560
And then meters squared times meter,

03:06.560 --> 03:08.210
we are left with cubic meters,

03:08.210 --> 03:10.190
which is exactly what they asked us for.

03:10.190 --> 03:15.190
And of course, we could rewrite
this as 2.4 cubic meters.

03:16.290 --> 03:18.193
And we are done.
